#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; is a vocabulary trainer. It helps you to memorize your vocabulary, "
"for example when you are trying to learn a foreign language. You can create "
"your own files with the words you need or select from a great variety of "
"files on its <ulink url=\"http://edu.kde.org/parley\">homepage</ulink>. "
"There you can find files containing language vocabulary and also anatomy, "
"music, geography, chemistry or exam preparation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; is very flexible and uses the flash card learning approach. It "
"automatically keeps track of your progress and lets you sort your vocabulary "
"as you wish. But unlike real flash cards you can use different learning "
"methods with &parley;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Flashcards contain expressions on the front side and their translation on "
"the back. You start with a pile of cards. If you know the translation on a "
"card, you can put it into a second pile of cards. If you fail, you keep it "
"in the first one to try again later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley;s main focus is not to teach you grammar or other sophisticated "
"things. However, there are some exercise forms which may help you in this "
"matter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Start to &parley;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&parley; main window</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&parley; main window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a start you could open an example file by using the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open Example...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu. There are 2 files which you may use in order "
"to get to know all the functions of &parley;. The file <filename>sample-en."
"kvtml</filename> e.g. shows you some vocabulary words in English, German and "
"French."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also download vocabulary files directly from the internet using "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Download New Vocabularies...</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Get Vocabularies dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Get Vocabularies dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, for example, I choose the file \"Basic vocabulary German-English\" "
"with a click on the <guibutton>Install</guibutton> button in the dialog, the "
"file is saved in your home dir ~/Vocabularies."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Basic vocabulary German-English file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "The vocabulary file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left of the main window you see a list of lessons. To select a lesson "
"for training tick the box in front of it. After selecting one or more "
"lessons let's start learning by clicking <guimenu>Start Practice</guimenu> "
"in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Written Practice Dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Written Practice Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After starting the practice &parley; asks you to enter a translation. Let's "
"assume that you are not too sure about it. Just click once on "
"<guibutton>Show More</guibutton> and the first letter of the word appears in "
"the entry box. Click again and the second letter shows up. If you prefer to "
"see the word completely, click on the <guibutton>Show Solution</guibutton> "
"button. If you want to check your answer click on <guibutton>Verify</"
"guibutton>. To ignore words or to mark them as known without entering them, "
"click on the <guibutton>Skip (Do Not Know)</guibutton> or <guibutton>Skip (I "
"know It)</guibutton> buttons respectively. In the progress box you the "
"number of words you have answered correctly and the seconds remaining for "
"your answer. You can configure this option in the <guibutton>configure "
"practice</guibutton> <guimenuitem>Advanced</guimenuitem> settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case you find writing the words too hard, why not try a multiple choice "
"test? After stopping the practice click on <guimenuitem>Configure Practice</"
"guimenuitem> and choose a different practice method. You can also change the "
"order of languages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Configure Practice Dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Configure Practice Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is how a <guimenuitem>Multiple Choice Test</guimenuitem> looks like:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Multiple Choice Practice Dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Multiple Choice Practice Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &parley;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the main window of &parley;. It consists of two areas: the lesson "
"list in the left third of the window and the current vocabulary list in the "
"other two thirds."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:192 index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr "Ecran"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "The lesson list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The lesson list on the left shows all lessons in your vocabulary file. If "
"you mark a lesson, is will become the current one. In this case it is "
"survival training."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The ticked box left of the name of each lesson indicates that it is to be "
"included in the practice. You may choose as many lessons for a test as you "
"like."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On top of the list there is a combo box which allows you to select which "
"vocabulary selection you want displayed on the right:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "The current lesson only (survival training in this case)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lessons in the test (the ones with a checkmark)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "All lessons (everything in the vocabulary file)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "The vocabulary list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on your selection, one or more lessons are displayed on the right "
"side of the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A green check mark in the second column means that this entry is active. A "
"red and white \"X\" indicates a deactivated entry that will not be "
"practiced. See Editing Entries for more information on active entries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you mark a range of entries to work with, their background colour "
"changes. Many editing functions work for multiple entries simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The colour in the column with the original will vary if you have two or more "
"columns with translations. If the cursor is in one of the translations the "
"colour represents its grade <quote>to the original</quote>. See section "
"<link linkend=\"entry6-dlg\">entry dialog</link> for more on this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Of course it is also possible to use the vocabulary list as an ordinary "
"dictionary and <link linkend=\"smart-search\"> to look up manually</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "The search bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "The search bar is located above the vocabulary table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the search bar to filter your vocabulary. If you type in a "
"string, you will only see entries with this string in the vocabulary table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "The status bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The status bar is located at the bottom of the main window. It contains:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "word type (for example: noun/verb/adjective)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"pronunciation. You can use <acronym>IPA</acronym> characters from the "
"phonetic alphabet. See more about this in the according <link linkend=\"opt-"
"dlg-ipa\">options dialog page</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "an additional comment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the keyboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can access &parley;s full functionality with the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Tab</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor is moved to the smart search input field. If you start typing an "
"expression in this field, &parley; will search the next best match after "
"each key. The cursor in the vocabulary is then moved to this location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you press <keycap>Return</keycap> it will move to the next match."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you only want entries that match from the <emphasis>beginning</emphasis> "
"of the expression you must press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl; "
"<keycap>Return</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift; <keycap>Tab</keycap></keycombo> "
"or <keycap>Tab</keycap> will move back to the vocabulary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycap>Right Arrow</keycap>, <keycap>Left Arrow</keycap>, <keycap>Up Arrow</"
"keycap>, <keycap>Down Arrow</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor moves inside the vocabulary table one column or line accordingly. "
"If it reaches the edge of the vocabulary table, it will not move."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Page Up</keycap>, <keycap>Page Down</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor in the vocabulary is moved up or down one page (the amount of "
"visible lines -1). If it has to jump beyond the edge of the vocabulary "
"table, it will not move."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;<keycap>Return</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Invokes the <guilabel>Edit Properties</guilabel> dialogue for this entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Ins</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Appends a new row at the end of the vocabulary. The cursor jumps into the "
"<guilabel>Original</guilabel> row. You may type your entry right away or "
"invoke the <guilabel>Edit Properties</guilabel> dialogue for modification of "
"this entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have selected smart appending you will be prompted to enter "
"expressions in the original language and their translations until you stop "
"by pressing the ESC key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Del</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After confirmation in a safety dialogue, the current row or selection is "
"removed from the vocabulary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></keycombo> or <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By pressing &Ctrl; and <keycap>+</keycap> or <keycap>-</keycap>, you can "
"choose the previous or next item in the combo box determining the current "
"lesson."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "Double clicking in a field in the table lets you edit this field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<mousebutton>Left</mousebutton> mouse click on one of the header buttons "
"will sort this column in ascending order. Another click will sort it in "
"descending order. In case the column is displayed in alphabetical order, you "
"can see a triangle at the end of the button showing the sorting direction."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keeping the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> mouse button pressed for about 1 "
"second on one of the table header buttons will pop up its <link linkend="
"\"header-menu\">header menu</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working on selections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you mark several expressions, you can modify their properties together or "
"save the selection as a new file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click on an entry, its row will be marked. Keeping the &Ctrl; key "
"pressed while clicking on another entry, will add its row to your selection. "
"By pressing the &Shift; key and clicking on a row further away from your "
"selection will add all rows in between to your selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The edit dialog has a different appearance for selections. Some properties "
"are disabled as it doesn't make sense to edit the expressions themselves or "
"remarks of a whole range simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All fields which may be modified are empty at the beginning to represent "
"their unmodified state. Modifications of properties will only be saved if "
"you confirm them by clicking on the <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available file formats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid "&parley; can read and write the following file formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"its native xml-style document type with the extension <literal role="
"\"extension\">.kvtml</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to share documents with others, use this format as it is the "
"only file format that is capable of storing <emphasis>all</emphasis> "
"properties in &parley;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"simple text files with special delimiters between the entries which are also "
"used by simple database programs. The extension is <literal role=\"extension"
"\">.csv</literal> in this case."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a lot of files on the Internet which use the tab stops or one or "
"two colons to separate the languages. To select this separator use the tab "
"for setting the <link linkend=\"options4-dlg\"><guilabel> Copy &amp; Paste</"
"guilabel> options</link> in the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure &parley;...</guimenuitem> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; reads the first few bytes of a file and guesses its file format. If "
"none of the special types like <literal role=\"extension\">.kvtml</literal> "
"or <literal role=\"extension\">.lex</literal> are recognized, it will try "
"the <literal role=\"extension\">.csv</literal> format."
msgstr ""

