#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid "And how should I learn?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The usual way to learn with &parley; is to use one of its random query "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It keeps track of your knowledge of the expressions by assigning them to one "
"of seven levels ranging from <quote>Level 1</quote> to <quote>Level 7</"
"quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Several options are implemented which can be configured in the dialogue for "
"the query options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To keep the amount of expressions in a query in a reasonable range, you may "
"restrict it to one lesson and/or a certain word type. Research in psychology "
"of learning suggests that the number of entries in one lesson should not "
"exceed about 30."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The range of a query can depend on the current grade, the number of queries "
"and the last query date."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Learning is efficient if you repeat new vocabulary in growing intervals. "
"There is a blocking and expiring mechanism for that case, so that you are "
"not obliged to modify the settings after each cycle. Correctly answered "
"expressions are blocked at least for the given time and will only be shown "
"after the period of time defined as expiration time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The direction of the learning can be switched randomly to avoid one way "
"learning only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For your personal taste or just for becoming acquainted with a new word, you "
"may choose a query that shows the solution together with several other "
"randomly chosen words. This is called multiple choice query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Special word types need special queries. For this reason there are queries "
"for the conjugation of verbs, comparison form of adjectives and the articles "
"of nouns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All these settings can be summarized into <link linkend=\"profiles"
"\">profiles</link> and retained under an arbitrary name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When querying, &parley; shows the expressions in random order until you "
"confirm all as <quote>known</quote>. If you did not select a special lesson, "
"all lessons are queried one after the other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you leave &parley;, expressions left in a running query are stored "
"accordingly. At a later restart you can resume the query (this does not "
"apply to special queries with verbs, articles and comparisons at the "
"moment). Those expressions are marked with a green check mark in the <link "
"linkend=\"overview\">main view</link>."
msgstr ""

