#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After entering a new language code in the field to its left, you use this "
"button to append it to your list. After that you need to fill in the fields "
"for the long name and the picture for the header button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:956
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Language Data From KDE Database"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:957
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on this drop down box opens a list that contains all the countries "
"that are known in your &kde; installation. Ordered by country you can add "
"your desired language properties to your personal list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:961
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Maybe you want to change the language name or the according picture but I "
"strongly recommend you keep at least the 2-byte language code and its 3-byte "
"alternative if you do not have a special reason. This is to achieve "
"compatible document files that can be shared among all users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:969
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Language Data From ISO639-1"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on this drop down box opens a list that contains all the language "
"codes that are covered by <quote>ISO639-1</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:978
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Basically the previous two drop down boxes provide the same data. The former "
"contains the language codes known in &kde; sorted by country whereas the "
"second contains <emphasis>all</emphasis> <quote>ISO639-1</quote> codes "
"sorted alphabetically."
msgstr ""

